WEBVTT

00:00:12.290 --> 00:00:14.820
Kagami...

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:17.820
Kagami!

00:00:23.870 --> 00:00:26.670
There are numerous articles
of clothing scattered about,

00:00:26.670 --> 00:00:29.570
but no people in sight.

00:00:29.570 --> 00:00:34.180
Those at the scene report that it's as
if everyone instantaneously disappeared.

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:36.980
- Nataru, you're all right?!
- Currently, no one is allowed into the coastal area,

00:00:36.980 --> 00:00:42.920
- Dad... I was there.
- and the Coast Guard, the
Metropolitan Police, and the SDF

00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:44.690
- Nataru...
- are working to seal off the
site and confirm any survivors.

00:00:44.690 --> 00:00:45.590
- But I survived when no one else did.

00:00:45.590 --> 00:00:47.260
- As of yet none of
the above have any comment.

00:00:47.260 --> 00:00:48.760
- But I survived when no one else did.

00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:49.750
- I...
- We'll let you know as soon as...

00:00:50.690 --> 00:00:52.700
<i>Say goodbye, hello</i>

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:57.900
<i>Then we repeat, going</i>
<i>eternally round and round</i>

00:00:57.900 --> 00:01:05.410
<i>Where will our path lead?</i>

00:01:05.410 --> 00:01:11.910
<i>What do I lose sight of when I'm with you?</i>

00:01:11.910 --> 00:01:19.590
<i>A colorful array of love and kindness</i>

00:01:19.590 --> 00:01:26.300
<i>I've remembered what</i>
<i>I'd forgotten since the days</i>

00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:32.600
<i>when we hurt each other over trivial things</i>

00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:39.910
<i>The sounds of our footsteps are</i>
<i>the "tracks" that lead to the future</i>

00:01:39.910 --> 00:01:47.580
<i>Within the ever-changing scenery... always</i>

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:49.620
<i>Say goodbye, hello</i>

00:01:49.620 --> 00:01:54.720
<i>Then we repeat, going</i>
<i>eternally round and round</i>

00:01:54.720 --> 00:02:01.760
<i>This melody that paints the future,</i>
<i>until the world changes</i>

00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:03.770
<i>Say goodbye, hello</i>

00:02:03.770 --> 00:02:09.010
<i>The sun always rises again,</i>
<i>eternally repeating its arc</i>

00:02:09.010 --> 00:02:19.850
<i>It lights up our path</i>

00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:52.470
"Let All Our Hearts Be One!"

00:03:06.800 --> 00:03:10.700
Mm-hmm, it turned out quite nicely, didn't it?

00:03:10.700 --> 00:03:15.200
Yes, we managed. Though I
was worried there for a while...

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:17.810
No, you worked hard.

00:03:17.810 --> 00:03:19.540
Hayamiya!

00:03:19.540 --> 00:03:21.580
We borrowed the projector.

00:03:21.580 --> 00:03:25.250
Right, thanks. Adjust it later, okay?

00:03:25.250 --> 00:03:26.680
Okay.

00:03:29.250 --> 00:03:31.990
I seem to remember your
presentation is tomorrow?

00:03:31.990 --> 00:03:33.560
Yes, that's right.

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:36.760
We're counting on you, Senkawa.
If you mess up with the projector,

00:03:36.760 --> 00:03:40.700
my presentation will be wasted.

00:03:40.700 --> 00:03:42.100
I know, jeez.

00:03:42.100 --> 00:03:43.930
We're all set!

00:03:45.570 --> 00:03:48.000
Um, the first on shift are...

00:03:49.240 --> 00:03:51.070
You and Sudou.

00:03:51.070 --> 00:03:54.840
So we have free time until it's time to switch off.

00:03:54.840 --> 00:03:57.380
Let's go see the other classes' stuff.

00:03:57.380 --> 00:04:02.750
Yay! I want to go to the Drag Café
that Class 3-G is doing.

00:04:02.750 --> 00:04:06.420
Kitamura, you have really extreme tastes.

00:04:06.420 --> 00:04:08.360
Aw, doesn't it sound fun?

00:04:08.360 --> 00:04:11.190
- Let's go see what our class is doing.
- You'd better be back in an hour!

00:04:14.600 --> 00:04:16.130
They're really going at it.

00:04:16.130 --> 00:04:17.960
Everybody's working hard.

00:04:19.470 --> 00:04:21.140
That tasted so-so.

00:04:21.140 --> 00:04:24.310
You're unexpectedly blunt, Kitamura.

00:04:24.310 --> 00:04:25.880
Hey, fortunetelling!

00:04:25.880 --> 00:04:27.540
Oh, yeah, that's Class E.

00:04:27.540 --> 00:04:29.530
Come on, let's check it out!

00:04:31.580 --> 00:04:34.050
Girls sure like stuff like that, huh?

00:04:34.050 --> 00:04:35.040
Yeah.

00:04:36.720 --> 00:04:38.450
One, please!

00:04:38.450 --> 00:04:39.890
Go ahead!

00:04:42.260 --> 00:04:43.250
"36"

00:04:43.430 --> 00:04:45.430
That's Number 36!

00:04:45.430 --> 00:04:47.260
Number 36!

00:04:47.260 --> 00:04:48.460
"Fortune"
"Fortune"
Here.

00:04:48.460 --> 00:04:49.090
"Fortune"

00:04:49.500 --> 00:04:50.490
Let's see.

00:04:51.270 --> 00:04:52.260
"Very Good Luck"

00:04:52.400 --> 00:04:53.970
Very good luck!

00:04:53.970 --> 00:04:55.570
"You lucky thing,

00:04:55.570 --> 00:05:00.940
this year you're gonna get a big,
cool, hot, cute significant other!"

00:05:00.940 --> 00:05:03.150
Wow, awesome!

00:05:03.150 --> 00:05:05.410
You don't have to take it seriously...

00:05:05.410 --> 00:05:07.150
But it seems kind of fun.

00:05:07.150 --> 00:05:09.140
What, you're going to do this?

00:05:11.490 --> 00:05:12.480
"52"

00:05:12.760 --> 00:05:14.660
That's Number 52!

00:05:14.660 --> 00:05:16.460
Number 52!

00:05:16.460 --> 00:05:16.530
"Fortune"
Number 52!

00:05:16.530 --> 00:05:17.760
Here.
"Fortune"

00:05:17.760 --> 00:05:18.090
"Fortune"

00:05:18.460 --> 00:05:19.100
"Very Bad Luck"

00:05:19.100 --> 00:05:20.360
Very bad luck?!
"Very Bad Luck"

00:05:20.360 --> 00:05:22.300
It says "You're descended from aliens.
"Very Bad Luck"

00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:22.500
It says "You're descended from aliens.

00:05:22.500 --> 00:05:27.640
Eventually you'll find out the secret of your birth!"

00:05:27.640 --> 00:05:29.470
You're taking it seriously, too.

00:05:29.470 --> 00:05:34.780
I'll be your friend even if
you <i>are</i> an alien or something.

00:05:34.780 --> 00:05:37.050
Go on, Senkawa, it's your turn next.

00:05:37.050 --> 00:05:38.610
I have to do it, too?

00:05:38.610 --> 00:05:40.010
Hurry up!

00:05:42.550 --> 00:05:45.320
You can do it if you want.

00:05:45.320 --> 00:05:48.960
This is called a "fortune," and
it's basically testing your luck.

00:05:48.960 --> 00:05:50.230
If the paper says something good,

00:05:50.230 --> 00:05:52.220
it can make you feel better than you'd think.

00:05:53.630 --> 00:05:54.620
"Very Good Luck"

00:05:54.660 --> 00:05:56.630
Very good luck! Cool!

00:05:56.630 --> 00:06:00.570
It says "You'll have a fated reunion
with the one you've been longing for"!

00:06:00.570 --> 00:06:03.040
Do you have someone you've
been wanting to see, Senkawa?

00:06:03.040 --> 00:06:06.210
Huh? Not really...

00:06:06.210 --> 00:06:07.200
Tsutomu!

00:06:10.180 --> 00:06:11.170
Nakasugi!

00:06:12.920 --> 00:06:15.320
That's in the past now...

00:06:15.320 --> 00:06:17.310
- Hang in there, Senkawa!
- What's wrong?

00:06:18.890 --> 00:06:21.080
Please fill out our survey!

00:06:25.260 --> 00:06:27.500
I'm sorry.

00:06:27.500 --> 00:06:30.070
Sorry I didn't want to help at first.

00:06:30.070 --> 00:06:35.940
Frankly, I didn't realize you
were thinking this seriously.

00:06:35.940 --> 00:06:38.910
Hey... do you remember?

00:06:38.910 --> 00:06:41.040
When we were interviewing at the refugee camp.

00:06:41.040 --> 00:06:47.680
You told me "Let's make something
good and show it to lots of people."

00:06:47.680 --> 00:06:52.390
Um... Well, I felt... You know...

00:06:52.390 --> 00:06:54.260
We're back!

00:06:54.260 --> 00:06:55.360
Welcome back!

00:06:55.360 --> 00:06:56.790
Aren't you early?

00:06:56.790 --> 00:06:59.960
What's with the attitude?
We came back early for you!

00:06:59.960 --> 00:07:01.860
Huh? Where's Senkawa?

00:07:01.860 --> 00:07:04.930
He said he felt sick and went up to the roof.

00:07:04.930 --> 00:07:06.270
Oh...

00:07:06.270 --> 00:07:07.370
Okay.

00:07:07.370 --> 00:07:09.740
Let's all wander around and check stuff out.

00:07:09.740 --> 00:07:11.740
Um, the next shift is...

00:07:11.740 --> 00:07:13.980
Oh, that's me and Masakubo.

00:07:13.980 --> 00:07:16.910
Come to think of it, where
are Masakubo and Hazawa?

00:07:16.910 --> 00:07:19.320
Just then, an old lady in sandals said...

00:07:19.320 --> 00:07:21.150
"You saw me!"

00:07:23.290 --> 00:07:25.220
Hey, that wasn't a joke!

00:07:25.220 --> 00:07:27.320
But you suck at this!

00:07:27.320 --> 00:07:29.310
- Yeah!
- What?!

00:07:31.730 --> 00:07:34.760
A fated reunion with the one I want to see, huh?

00:07:34.760 --> 00:07:39.570
Oh, but I guess you
picked this fortune, huh Birdy?

00:07:39.570 --> 00:07:41.800
The one you want to see...

00:07:41.800 --> 00:07:45.410
Oh, right, the one who
saved you at Central Tower...

00:07:45.410 --> 00:07:47.410
Stop it.

00:07:47.410 --> 00:07:49.240
I'll kill every last one.

00:07:51.450 --> 00:07:56.620
I couldn't do a thing.
Not catch him... or even chase him.

00:07:56.620 --> 00:07:57.320
"Very Good Luck"
I couldn't do a thing.
Not catch him... or even chase him.

00:07:57.320 --> 00:07:59.020
I don't think it was your fault.
"Very Good Luck"

00:07:59.020 --> 00:07:59.790
I don't think it was your fault.

00:07:59.790 --> 00:08:05.130
Nataru was your childhood friend,
and cheerful, and a good person.

00:08:05.130 --> 00:08:07.600
It was a lie.

00:08:07.600 --> 00:08:09.500
It was all a lie!

00:08:09.500 --> 00:08:12.840
And I couldn't see through it.

00:08:12.840 --> 00:08:16.440
You don't want to believe it even now, right?

00:08:16.440 --> 00:08:17.840
I was like that, too.

00:08:19.480 --> 00:08:22.780
When we found out Nakasugi was the Ryunka,

00:08:22.780 --> 00:08:24.380
I couldn't believe it either.

00:08:24.380 --> 00:08:26.210
I didn't want to believe it.

00:08:27.680 --> 00:08:29.950
I got in your way...

00:08:29.950 --> 00:08:32.190
You were brave, Tsutomu.

00:08:32.190 --> 00:08:34.020
I was just in a frenzy.

00:08:38.030 --> 00:08:43.800
At the time, losing Nakasugi seemed
like it would mean losing myself...

00:08:43.800 --> 00:08:45.840
I guess I was just so excited.

00:08:45.840 --> 00:08:50.810
It was the first time just being with
someone had made me feel at ease...

00:08:50.810 --> 00:08:54.840
And like we understood each
other without even speaking...

00:08:54.840 --> 00:09:00.980
It wasn't really "love" or
some big deal like that, but...

00:09:00.980 --> 00:09:04.690
Nataru must be like that for you, too.

00:09:04.690 --> 00:09:07.090
He kissed you.

00:09:10.260 --> 00:09:12.190
Who kissed who, now?

00:09:12.190 --> 00:09:14.000
M-Mr. Muroto?

00:09:14.000 --> 00:09:17.900
Long time no see, Senkawa. Hey, you okay?

00:09:17.900 --> 00:09:20.770
Got more youth than you know
what to do with, or something?

00:09:20.770 --> 00:09:22.670
What are you doing here?

00:09:22.670 --> 00:09:27.710
Hey, I'm an old Journalism Club
boy coming to see my juniors' work,

00:09:27.710 --> 00:09:29.450
and you're being so cold!

00:09:29.450 --> 00:09:34.080
Back in the day, I used to come
here to skip class all the time, too.

00:09:34.080 --> 00:09:37.720
Well, be <i>careful:</i> if you skip
too much you'll end up like me...

00:09:37.720 --> 00:09:39.720
Huh?

00:09:39.720 --> 00:09:40.920
Senkawa?

00:09:44.260 --> 00:09:47.250
Guess he doesn't want to listen to an old man...

00:09:50.100 --> 00:09:51.630
Sh-Shion Arita?!

00:09:51.630 --> 00:09:53.700
What are you doing here?

00:09:53.700 --> 00:09:56.710
Where's Nataru?

00:09:56.710 --> 00:09:58.900
He's still staying with you, isn't he?

00:10:02.080 --> 00:10:05.110
I got a car. I'm about to head back.

00:10:05.110 --> 00:10:07.950
Good. We'll see you at the meeting place.

00:10:13.820 --> 00:10:18.890
Do you know why I chose this planet for our escape?

00:10:18.890 --> 00:10:21.060
It's because I wanted to see with my own eyes

00:10:21.060 --> 00:10:24.130
the scar the Ryunka left.

00:10:24.130 --> 00:10:26.300
It'd be fair to call this
weapon the ultimate deterrent,

00:10:26.300 --> 00:10:28.440
but the Federation sealed it away.

00:10:28.440 --> 00:10:31.840
Even though the threat of
the Union is ever-present...

00:10:31.840 --> 00:10:35.310
Those fools who've become slack in
this false peace don't understand...

00:10:35.310 --> 00:10:38.250
the Federation needs the Ryunka.

00:10:38.250 --> 00:10:40.440
But I've had enough now.

00:11:00.870 --> 00:11:02.940
I'll kill you here.

00:11:02.940 --> 00:11:05.310
You may be an lxioran,
but you're still just an Altan.

00:11:05.310 --> 00:11:07.710
I'll kill you just like I killed Dusk.

00:11:23.060 --> 00:11:27.300
I'll kill you... You, above all others...

00:11:27.300 --> 00:11:29.130
I'll finish you off now.

00:11:31.700 --> 00:11:32.890
Why, you!

00:11:40.680 --> 00:11:41.670
I'll kill you!

00:11:52.020 --> 00:11:54.010
I let him get away...

00:12:12.670 --> 00:12:14.710
He's a monster.

00:12:14.710 --> 00:12:19.080
If we don't dispose of him quickly, we'll be goners.

00:12:19.080 --> 00:12:20.510
I agree.

00:12:21.250 --> 00:12:26.240
He's sure to come here. When he does, we'll...

00:12:27.890 --> 00:12:29.960
Moss?

00:12:29.960 --> 00:12:32.030
You've gotten old.

00:12:32.030 --> 00:12:34.020
I hate weak men.

00:12:40.600 --> 00:12:42.430
Farewell, Colonel.

00:12:55.950 --> 00:12:57.390
Gatol is dead.

00:12:57.390 --> 00:12:58.750
Where's the proof?

00:12:58.750 --> 00:13:00.920
It's his mimesis chip.

00:13:00.920 --> 00:13:03.920
If you look at the data, you should see everything.

00:13:07.400 --> 00:13:11.900
In the end, even Wolf of Kaltago
was taken down easily, eh?

00:13:11.900 --> 00:13:15.670
I did what you asked. I'd like
you to put me through to Revi.

00:13:15.670 --> 00:13:20.580
I'm sorry to say that Revi doesn't wish to see you.

00:13:20.580 --> 00:13:23.680
That wasn't the deal! You said if I
killed Gatol you'd let me meet Revi!

00:13:23.680 --> 00:13:27.480
You lot were the ones who first broke the deal.

00:13:27.480 --> 00:13:32.820
You experimented on the Ryunka
without giving us the precise data.

00:13:32.820 --> 00:13:38.660
We didn't want the life
forms of this planet eradicated!

00:13:38.660 --> 00:13:41.300
It's the kind of thing the military
would come up with, though...

00:13:41.300 --> 00:13:43.970
It goes to show we were careless.

00:13:43.970 --> 00:13:47.600
I'll tell the Federation that Revi is on Earth.

00:13:47.600 --> 00:13:49.430
Do as you like.

00:13:52.270 --> 00:13:54.870
We will never meet again.

00:14:01.720 --> 00:14:04.710
Well, fine. I can do what I like now.

00:14:11.290 --> 00:14:14.300
He did leave the apartment for a while yesterday,

00:14:14.300 --> 00:14:18.030
but he came back before long, dead-tired.

00:14:18.030 --> 00:14:19.700
How's he been today?

00:14:19.700 --> 00:14:24.210
He's been sleeping in his room
all day. He seems pretty sick.

00:14:24.210 --> 00:14:25.640
Are you...

00:14:27.740 --> 00:14:29.970
Don't break my lock again, okay?

00:14:32.380 --> 00:14:34.480
Please...

00:14:34.480 --> 00:14:36.880
Let me go in alone.

00:14:38.420 --> 00:14:41.250
Please. Alone.

00:14:54.270 --> 00:14:56.510
Nataru?!

00:14:56.510 --> 00:14:57.840
What's wrong?

00:14:57.840 --> 00:15:01.410
Snap out of it, Nataru! Nataru!

00:15:01.410 --> 00:15:03.180
Birdy...

00:15:03.180 --> 00:15:08.220
I can't let you catch me yet.

00:15:08.220 --> 00:15:14.210
Not yet... Not until I kill them... three left...

00:15:15.620 --> 00:15:17.390
Don't talk anymore!

00:15:17.390 --> 00:15:18.790
Nataru!

00:15:22.360 --> 00:15:23.760
Lailalo.

00:15:27.040 --> 00:15:30.230
Why do I have to wait like
this in front of my own place?

00:15:31.770 --> 00:15:34.610
Miss Arita, I'm coming in!

00:15:36.110 --> 00:15:37.100
Huh?!

00:15:38.780 --> 00:15:40.610
They disappeared...

00:15:57.300 --> 00:15:59.430
How long was I out?

00:15:59.430 --> 00:16:01.140
A whole day.

00:16:01.140 --> 00:16:06.140
I ordered Lailalo to give you the tuning you need.

00:16:06.140 --> 00:16:08.140
I checked your body.

00:16:08.140 --> 00:16:14.350
Oh. So you found out that I'm an lxioran, then.

00:16:14.350 --> 00:16:16.320
I never thought there'd be an lxioran

00:16:16.320 --> 00:16:18.120
outside the supervision of
the Federation government...

00:16:18.120 --> 00:16:21.120
I'm defective goods. My initial tuning failed.

00:16:21.120 --> 00:16:23.090
I was a reject.

00:16:23.090 --> 00:16:29.970
Some Isdalta members stole me from
a Cephon lab without knowing that.

00:16:29.970 --> 00:16:33.140
And Dusk took you in, right?

00:16:33.140 --> 00:16:34.640
Yeah.

00:16:34.640 --> 00:16:37.940
Dad left the organization after that.

00:16:37.940 --> 00:16:40.480
In order to raise me.

00:16:40.480 --> 00:16:43.110
And I wasn't told anything.

00:16:43.110 --> 00:16:46.720
So I lived as a normal Altan.

00:16:46.720 --> 00:16:52.190
Back on Oriotera, and here on Earth, too.

00:16:52.190 --> 00:16:54.190
That day...

00:16:54.190 --> 00:16:57.690
Kagami died right before my eyes.

00:16:57.690 --> 00:17:02.500
The others around me, too.
I was the only one who survived...

00:17:02.500 --> 00:17:04.490
Thanks to my power as an lxioran.

00:17:07.240 --> 00:17:08.670
Why?

00:17:08.670 --> 00:17:10.070
Why <i>now?</i>

00:17:13.640 --> 00:17:15.710
I can't believe I'm an lxioran...

00:17:15.710 --> 00:17:19.150
Never use that power, Nataru.

00:17:21.720 --> 00:17:24.050
The Ryunka got your...

00:17:24.050 --> 00:17:28.860
The power sleeping within me
awoke so that I could survive.

00:17:28.860 --> 00:17:30.830
I can even jump.

00:17:30.830 --> 00:17:32.830
I'm a real monster.

00:17:32.830 --> 00:17:34.430
Nataru...

00:17:34.430 --> 00:17:39.030
Birdy, we lxiorans...

00:17:39.030 --> 00:17:42.200
...should never have been born.

00:17:42.200 --> 00:17:46.580
We're weapons created by the ancient Empire!

00:17:46.580 --> 00:17:48.010
We're not people.

00:17:50.880 --> 00:17:52.070
Nataru...

00:17:53.420 --> 00:17:56.350
But it's not over yet.

00:17:56.350 --> 00:17:58.340
I'll kill them all.

00:18:01.690 --> 00:18:03.630
Nataru!

00:18:03.630 --> 00:18:06.060
The target has vanished. He jumped.

00:18:09.930 --> 00:18:11.760
Birdy Cephon, you're being called.

00:18:12.270 --> 00:18:15.900
I don't know why you'd turn yourself in <i>now.</i>

00:18:15.900 --> 00:18:18.440
I decided to withdraw from this game.

00:18:18.440 --> 00:18:20.910
I'm tired of running all the time, for one thing.

00:18:20.910 --> 00:18:22.240
Valic...

00:18:22.240 --> 00:18:25.780
Plus, I don't want to be killed by that lxioran.

00:18:25.780 --> 00:18:28.880
Now hurry up and take me to Oriotera.

00:18:28.880 --> 00:18:33.490
I won't talk about what happened
without a lawyer present, though.

00:18:33.490 --> 00:18:36.220
Hmph, you're a sharp operator.

00:18:36.220 --> 00:18:40.230
I'm going to make you talk about
the Central Tower terrorism, too,

00:18:40.230 --> 00:18:41.300
Valic Nigua.

00:18:41.300 --> 00:18:42.500
Huh?

00:18:42.500 --> 00:18:44.900
Jeez, that again?

00:18:44.900 --> 00:18:49.740
You're sure obsessed with that old story.

00:18:49.740 --> 00:18:54.910
The guy after me was involved
in that incident too, you know.

00:18:54.910 --> 00:18:59.950
That defective lxioran was there.

00:18:59.950 --> 00:19:05.150
I never thought he'd become
a <i>real</i> lxioran one day, though.

00:19:15.330 --> 00:19:17.100
Is this Moss Kiri?

00:19:17.100 --> 00:19:19.370
I've been waiting for you, Nataru.

00:19:19.370 --> 00:19:21.670
Why doesn't Gatol answer?

00:19:21.670 --> 00:19:24.540
He died.

00:19:24.540 --> 00:19:26.480
Did you kill him?

00:19:26.480 --> 00:19:28.710
I hate weak men.

00:19:28.710 --> 00:19:32.650
A falling-out, eh? Well, you're next, then.

00:19:32.650 --> 00:19:35.720
Yes. I like strong men.

00:19:35.720 --> 00:19:37.550
Give me a good time, won't you?

00:19:43.860 --> 00:19:50.030
"And so we learned that there
are many different forms of love.

00:19:50.030 --> 00:19:55.840
As long as we have love, we humans
can overcome any difficulty..."

00:19:55.840 --> 00:19:57.570
Isn't this "love" stuff kinda cheesy?

00:19:57.570 --> 00:19:59.170
Eh, it's fine.

00:19:59.170 --> 00:20:02.880
Wow, I wouldn't have figured you for a romantic.

00:20:02.880 --> 00:20:04.150
Shut up.

00:20:04.150 --> 00:20:08.850
It's gonna start in ten minutes.
You can't change your script <i>now!</i>

00:20:08.850 --> 00:20:10.480
You're right, but...

00:20:15.890 --> 00:20:19.390
Wh-Wh-What should I do? The room's packed!

00:20:19.390 --> 00:20:21.000
That's a good thing.

00:20:21.000 --> 00:20:23.200
Oh, no, I'm getting nervous.

00:20:23.200 --> 00:20:25.030
Isn't it a little late for that?

00:20:25.030 --> 00:20:28.070
Hayamiya! She's here!

00:20:28.070 --> 00:20:29.740
Come on, hurry.

00:20:29.740 --> 00:20:31.210
I made it in time!

00:20:31.210 --> 00:20:32.510
Nakasugi!

00:20:32.510 --> 00:20:34.280
Long time no see, Hayamiya.

00:20:34.280 --> 00:20:35.910
You really came to see me!

00:20:35.910 --> 00:20:38.580
Yep! It's your big day, after all!

00:20:38.580 --> 00:20:40.250
Thanks!

00:20:40.250 --> 00:20:41.720
Have you settled in to life in Kobe?

00:20:41.720 --> 00:20:46.120
Yeah! It's a very pretty city, and...

00:20:46.120 --> 00:20:48.220
Isn't Senkawa here?

00:20:48.220 --> 00:20:51.890
Huh? No, he's not here yet.

00:20:51.890 --> 00:20:53.430
Oh.

00:20:53.430 --> 00:20:55.700
Dunno what's taking him so long...

00:20:55.700 --> 00:20:57.100
Hayamiya, come here for a sec.

00:20:57.100 --> 00:20:58.470
Huh? What is it?

00:20:58.470 --> 00:21:01.270
I found this packed in one of my boxes.

00:21:01.270 --> 00:21:04.870
Oh, yeah, the three of us used
to get these taken all the time!

00:21:04.870 --> 00:21:06.070
But these...

00:21:08.240 --> 00:21:11.240
Do you know what happened
between me and Senkawa?

00:21:28.960 --> 00:21:33.900
Nataru... really make my blood burn.

00:21:33.900 --> 00:21:39.100
I'll stay with you until all
the life drains out of you.

00:21:41.480 --> 00:21:46.310
<i>Only a love that's ended becomes a seed</i>

00:21:46.310 --> 00:21:52.510
<i>Next, a flower blooms</i>

00:22:04.100 --> 00:22:09.600
<i>If you hang your head like that,</i>
<i>you won't get any sunlight</i>

00:22:09.600 --> 00:22:15.140
<i>Look up at the blue sky so you'll grow taller!</i>

00:22:15.140 --> 00:22:20.820
<i>Let's pour a few tears from the watering can</i>

00:22:20.820 --> 00:22:26.810
<i>Eventually shoots will spring up</i>
<i>from somewhere in your heart</i>

00:22:29.460 --> 00:22:32.530
<i>Let's take life slowly</i>

00:22:32.530 --> 00:22:37.530
<i>A girl's dreams are neverending</i>

00:22:37.530 --> 00:22:43.740
<i>Ah, there's someone</i>
<i>out there waiting for you</i>

00:22:43.740 --> 00:22:48.580
<i>Only a love that's ended becomes a seed</i>

00:22:48.580 --> 00:22:55.250
<i>Next, a flower blooms</i>

00:22:55.250 --> 00:23:00.060
<i>Only a love that's ended becomes a seed</i>

00:23:00.060 --> 00:23:06.050
<i>Next, a flower blooms</i>

00:23:11.670 --> 00:23:15.340
<i>After Nataru's physical damage</i>
<i>was repaired in the tune-up tank,</i>

00:23:15.340 --> 00:23:20.010
<i>he headed to the escapees' hideout to kill Moss.</i>

00:23:20.010 --> 00:23:25.180
<i>Birdy finds out about this from</i>
<i>Valic and rushes to the scene.</i>

00:23:25.180 --> 00:23:27.280
<i>Though she senses that her face-off with Nataru</i>

00:23:27.280 --> 00:23:30.720
<i>will be the beginning of a new tragedy...</i>

00:23:33.250 --> 00:23:37.250
<i>Nataru, I want to believe that you're...</i>
